Great luck, I found a ring of invisibility on L1, and a ring of
polymorphing on level 2.  Cursed-just to add to the fun.  I didn't
know what the ring was, and shortly after this I killed a werejackal
who bit me. So, after I killed a dwarf zombie and morphed to a baby
silver dragon, I thought I had become a werecreature. The dragon was
fun, but not as much fun as the succubus I became a few levels later.
There were very odd things going on with my level (gaining and losing
quickly), so I'm not sure what that was about.  I stole a few things
as the succubus, and then turned into a trapper.  How boring. :)
Unfortunately, I had started as a monk, so I felt guilty when I
enveloped an orc.

I lasted for a while as a barbed devil, and should have equipped
myself with some armor at a used armor store I found, but I didn't, so
I died quickly later.  In the meantime, I summoned another barbed
devil for help, which was major cool, and kind of made up for the
overloaded chickatrice and raven I became next.  Not to worry, for I
was able to carry all my gear as the pony I became next, when I fell
through the trap-hole in level 6 to level 9(!).  A major consultation
with the oracle raised me to level 6, and THEN I had the bright idea
to drink from one of her fountains.

Heh.  When will I learn not to go around quaffing random fountains?

A water demon shows up and tosses a potion at me, but misses.  I
think, "Hey!  Here's a good idea.  Let's pick the potion back up and
throw it at the demon!  If it would have done good for him against me,
it will do good for me against him, right?"  Well, not if it's a
potion of blindness.

So, blind, I'm fighting a water demon, a baby naga hatchling, and a
fire ant.  The ant sets me on fire, and suddenly potions are exploding
all around me, spellbooks are burning, and I revert to human form and
see Juiblex start hitting me just about the time my potion of blinding
burns and blinds me again.

It doesn't really matter that I can't see, though, because all around
me are Juiblex's digestive processes making me ill.  Finally, I
die-though I can only think a little 6th-level monk made a poor meal.

Possessions, once identified, included a pair of jumping boots and an
unburnt spellbook of confuse monster.

Moral of the story: in dire straits, use those unidentified items!
Also, uncontrolled polymorphing is mad fun. ;)

